          %h2#groups Groups
          %p
            The modern mathematical terminology
            %em group
            is short for
            %em
              group of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetries"} symmetries
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "Klein+geometry#Klein1872"} Klein 1872
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %em groups
            are equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} connected
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
          %p
            In traditional literature this fact is fully appreciated typically only in rather advanced corners of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+theory"} group theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
          %p We begin in
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#1Groups"} 1-Groups
          %p
            with a discussion of the simplest case of ordinary discrete groups from this natural perspective of regarding them as pointed connected
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+1-types"} homotopy 1-types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-group"} infinity-group
            objects in general
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-toposes"} (infinity,1)-toposes
          %h3#model_layer Model Layer
          %h4#1Groups 1-Groups
          %h5#discrete_groups_as_pointed_connected_groupoids Discrete groups as pointed connected groupoids
          %p
            We discuss how, via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping+and+delooping"} looping and delooping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+groups"} discrete groups
            are equivalent to pointed connected
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
          %p Write
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                are
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphisms"} 1-morphisms
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
                between these and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"} 2-morphisms
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
                between those, which are nessecarily
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+groups"}> discrete groups
                ), also regarded as a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Grpd
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grpd^{\ast/}
                for the
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,1)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+objects"} pointed objects
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Grpd
                        %mrow
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi Grpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grpd_{\geq 1} \hookrightarrow Grpd
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+sub-%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} full sub-(2,1)-category
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} connected
                groupoids, those for which
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ≃
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 \simeq \ast
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Grp
                        %mrow
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grp^{\ast/}_{\geq 1}
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+objects"} pointed objects
                in connected groupoids.
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
