                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\pi_1)_{X,Y}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Grpd^{\ast/}((\mathbf{B}G,\ast),(\mathbf{B}H,\ast))
                    \\longrightarrow
                    Grp(G,H)
            %p is an equivalence.
            %p
              To see this, observe that, by definition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+objects"} pointed objects
              via the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/undercategory"} undercategory
              under the point, a morphism in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grpd^{\ast/}
              between groupoids of this form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}(-)
              is a diagram in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Grp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grp
              (unpointed) of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
